{
  "//": [
    "Real, reserved project IDs (created 2026-08-29, Phase 02 §1).",
    "",
    "⚠️ dev is 'splitsutra-dev-eac96', NOT 'splitsutra-dev'. The bare name was consumed by a",
    "failed `firebase projects:create` run that created the GCP project but errored before",
    "attaching Firebase, so the console appended a suffix when the project was recreated. The",
    "orphaned bare 'splitsutra-dev' GCP project still exists with no Firebase resources.",
    "",
    "🔴 The prod ID ends in '-prod' and MUST keep that suffix. firebase/seed/src/guard.ts has",
    "two layers: rule 1 refuses any project id ending in '-prod' with NO override flag, and",
    "rule 2 refuses anything not starting with 'demo-' unless --allow-real-project is typed.",
    "Renaming prod to something not ending in '-prod' silently downgrades it from the first",
    "protection to the second.",
    "",
    "Both projects are on the free Spark plan and STAY there until Phase 11 (docs/18 §1).",
    "The projects and their Firestore databases now exist, but hold no data: day-to-day work",
    "still runs on the local emulator suite, which needs a 'demo-' project id and never reads",
    "this file. Toggle apps/web/.env.local VITE_USE_EMULATORS to switch.",
    "",
    "Firestore (default) databases exist in BOTH projects: us-central1, Native mode, Standard",
    "edition, created 2026-08-29. That location is permanent and cannot be changed (Q4).",
    "",
    "Both start with closed rules. firestore.rules in this repo is the real boundary and has",
    "not been deployed to either project yet.",
    "",
    "The project-level Resource Location ID still reads [Not specified] in projects:list. That",
    "is the default location for Storage and Hosting, NOT the Firestore location — it is set",
    "separately, when the first Storage bucket is created."
  ],
  "projects": {
    "default": "splitsutra-dev-eac96",
    "dev": "splitsutra-dev-eac96",
    "prod": "splitsutra-prod"
  },
